# Cortecho configuration. Optional: `docker compose up -d` works with this file
# as downloaded (or with no file at all), then open the UI and follow Setup.
#
# READ THE THREE LAYERS in docs/configuration.md:
#   1. the values in "Upgrading an older install" are imported into SQLite once
#   2. the values in "Read every start" stay in the environment
#   3. every other behaviour setting is edited in the web UI (Settings / Echos / Setup)
#
# Add the Echo, the OpenAI key, the reply address, the time zone and every
# model or voice in the UI. After the first start, changing a value from group 1
# does nothing (the app warns at startup).

# IANA zone. It also sets the container clock.
TZ=UTC

# --- Read every start: an OpenAI-compatible server (optional) ---------------
# Must implement the Responses API, streaming speech and audio transcription.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# --- Read every start: tools (optional) -------------------------------------
# See docs/configuration.md. JSON in an env var is easy to break with quoting;
# prefer TOOLS_FILE with a mounted tools.json.
# TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
# TOOLS_ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE=
# HTTP_TOOL_ENDPOINTS={"weather":{"url":"http://192.168.1.10:8006/weather","description":"Current outdoor weather"}}
# HOME_ASSISTANT_URL=http://homeassistant.local:8123
# HOME_ASSISTANT_TOKEN=
# HOME_ASSISTANT_ALLOWED_SERVICES=light.turn_on,light.turn_off
# SHELL_TOOL_SCRIPTS={"backup_status":{"path":"/app/scripts/backup-status.sh","description":"Last backup result"}}
# TOOLS_FILE=/app/tools.json

# --- Read every start: MCP connectors (Settings → Connectors) ---------------
# The browser-facing URL; OAuth redirects come back to /api/mcp/oauth/callback.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://echo-agent.example.com
# Base64 of 32 random bytes: openssl rand -base64 32. Losing it = sign in again.
CORTECHO_SECRET_KEY=
# MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# MCP_CIMD_ENABLED=false

# --- Read every start: discovery (optional) ---------------------------------
# Comma-separated host:port additions to the network scan, for an Echo on
# another subnet. The scan itself only connects to private IPv4 addresses.
# DISCOVERY_EXTRA_TARGETS=192.168.1.60:26053

# --- Read every start: server (usually leave these) -------------------------
LOG_LEVEL=info
# DEBUG_AUDIO_DIR=/app/data/audio
# DEBUG_AUDIO_KEEP=20

# --- Upgrading an older install ---------------------------------------------
# Everything below used to be the first-start configuration. It is imported
# into SQLite once: on a fresh database, and (for the reply address) on the
# first start after an upgrade that never saved one. Afterwards it is ignored
# and the app warns while it is still set, so remove these lines after the
# first successful start and change the values in the UI instead.
#
# The Echo (one device named "Echo"; add more in Setup):
# ECHO_HOST=192.168.1.50
# ECHO_PORT=26053
# 32-byte base64 key. Leave empty for a plaintext link; the setup wizard sets
# one itself, and `npm run echo-set-key` is the CLI fallback.
# ECHO_API_KEY=
#
# The OpenAI key and the language/voice (stored write-only in data/app.db):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# STT_LANGUAGES=en
# TTS_VOICE=marin
#
# How the Echo reached this app before Settings → Network existed (never a
# public URL; the Echo downloads the reply with a plain HTTP request):
# REPLY_AUDIO_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:3000
